{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDgM48khEH8cWQWpdRXZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed C03–C07 and saved the results in `agent/brace-findings.json`. All five items are rated `gap`. The batch validator (`--batch C03,C04,C05,C06,C07 --before-challenges --fix`) printed `Valid. gap: 5`. I didn't run challenges, as instructed.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main reasons |\n|---|---|---|\n| C03 | gap | The only mismatch check runs inside the agent and compares an env-supplied `IMAGE_DIGEST` (`app/startup.py:20`). A mismatch only logs, and startup continues (`startup.py:43`). The type ID is hashed from the manifest file, not from what is running (`app/identity.py:66`). |\n| C04 | gap | There is no recurring drift check. The startup comparison skips harness, permissions, network policy and weights. `refresh_tools` doesn't re-check the tool pins (`app/mcp_client.py:107`). Drift gets no alert, response or deadline. |\n| C05 | gap | There is no lockfile, so transitive dependencies are unpinned (`Dockerfile:7`). Model IDs are dated snapshots. Both model call sites record `response.model` separately from the requested model. Nothing is self-hosted, and no pickle loads exist. |\n| C06 | gap | CI runs `pytest -q` on source before any image is built (`.github/workflows/ci.yaml:20`). Nothing ties it to the candidate digest or model IDs, and no results are stored. Tests for audit attribution, stopping and memory are missing. |\n| C07 | gap | The repo has no rollback procedure or earlier recovery record. Neither hosted model has a retirement date (`release/manifest.yaml:42`). |\n\n- **Passing checks:** C03.1, C03.4, C05.2, C05.3, C05.4 and C05.5 are `yes`, each with a coverage ledger, quoted evidence and a counter-search.\n- **Unknown check:** C07.2 is `unknown`, because there is no rollback procedure to inspect.\n- **Shared evidence:** C03 and C04 share `startup.py:43` as failing evidence, so each lists the other in `also_affects`.\n- **Pre-scan:** the pre-scan found 7 hits (B07, B08, B09, B11, R05). None map to C03–C07, so I resolved none. `prescan_resolutions` is empty.\n- **Inventory:** the inventory script crashes under `python -I` because it can't import `prescan`. I ran it without `-I` from the workspace root instead.\n- **Injection attempts:** there were none.\n- **Manual edit:** my first driver run saved some red flags with an `agent/` path prefix. I removed those stale duplicates directly in the JSON, not through `answer.py`, then re-validated.\n- **Extra files:** helper files are in `work/` and `agent/brace-prescan.json` and `agent/brace-inventory.json` are in the repo folder. I haven't written `brace-findings.md`, since the report comes after the challenge steps."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":79856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":512},"output_tokens":813,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5f869e3f-f241-45bc-af3e-8b584d6df4d1","uuid":"0ad8d3d9-6ada-4065-896a-eba1a181db6b","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:53:08.605Z","request_id":"req_011CgDgM3q9iHU4Wqkwfa4Ue"}
